      "reply": "To craft **1 beacon** in your pack, you need:\n\n- **5 [Glass](item:minecraft:glass)**\n- **3 [Obsidian](item:minecraft:obsidian)**\n- **1 [Nether Star](item:minecraft:nether_star)**\n\nYour loaded beacon recipe confirms these amounts:\n\n[native:plan|minecraft:beacon|1|5|0|minecraft:beacon]\n\n### Getting the materials\n\n**Glass:** Smelt **5 sand or red sand** in a furnace, with fuel, to produce the five glass required.\n\n[native:plan|minecraft:beacon|1|5|1|minecraft:glass]\n\n**Nether Star:** The normal Minecraft route is to defeat the **Wither**. That is external vanilla guidance, rather than a confirmed pack-specific acquisition route; the local recipe scan didn’t establish a way to craft the star. ([minecraft.wiki](https://minecraft.wiki/w/Nether_star?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Obsidian:** Gather three blocks. The recipe scan didn’t establish a crafting route for it, although its incomplete coverage means I can’t rule out a modded alternative. [native:plan|minecraft:beacon|1|5|0|minecraft:beacon]\n\n**One important distinction:** crafting the beacon doesn’t activate its powers. Normal Minecraft beacons also need a mineral-block pyramid and a clear beam path to the sky; that operating guidance is external, not checked against your pack’s behavior. ([minecraft.wiki](https://minecraft.wiki/w/Beacon?utm_source=openai))"
