      "reply": "**You currently have no active status effects.** The bonuses I can identify come from **Creative-mode reach modifiers and your held Diamond Sword**, rather than an active potion or beacon effect.\n\n### Reach bonuses: Creative mode\nBoth reach modifiers explicitly identify Creative mode as their source:\n\n| Attribute | Base | Bonus | Current total |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Block interaction range | 4.5 blocks | +0.5 blocks | **5 blocks** |\n| Entity interaction range | 3 blocks | +2 blocks | **5 blocks** |\n\nThese are separate bonuses for interacting with blocks and entities. [native:player_attribute:minecraft:player.block_interaction_range] [native:player_attribute:minecraft:player.entity_interaction_range]\n\n### Weapon bonuses: your held Diamond Sword\nYour sword supplies these modifiers **while in your main hand**:\n\n- **+6 attack damage.** Its tooltip shows **7 Attack Damage**.\n- **−2.4 attack speed** relative to your base of 4, leaving **1.6 attack speed**. The live attack-speed modifier matches the sword’s modifier. [world:item|player:682d6bb8-6e5c-4b6e-877b-ba2d54222fa5>minecraft/main#0@minecraft:diamond_sword] [native:player_attribute:minecraft:generic.attack_speed]\n\nIt also has **four enchantments, all at level 100**:\n- Sharpness\n- Looting\n- Unbreaking\n- Mending\n\nThese are enchantments on the weapon, not timed effects on you. [world:item|player:682d6bb8-6e5c-4b6e-877b-ba2d54222fa5>minecraft/main#0@minecraft:diamond_sword]\n\n**Damage-reading caveat:** the client’s attack-damage attribute is not synchronized and reports only 1 with no modifiers, so that read cannot establish your actual server-side damage. The sword itself confirms its +6 modifier and 7-damage tooltip; I’m **not treating 7 as your final damage including Sharpness 100**. [native:player_attribute:minecraft:generic.attack_damage] [world:item|player:682d6bb8-6e5c-4b6e-877b-ba2d54222fa5>minecraft/main#0@minecraft:diamond_sword]\n\nThe above covers every modifier returned by the attribute check and every enchantment on your held sword. I’ve omitted the unchanged baseline attributes because they do not identify additional bonuses."
